Plot some level curves in the rectangle."},{"x":0.08775,"y":0.4751,"w":0.28363,"h":0.04229,"fs":0.03581,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"14.8 Lagrange Multipliers"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.52381,"w":0.59307,"h":0.07566,"fs":0.01279,"n":5,"k":1,"t":"Sometimes we need to find the extreme values of a function whose domain is constrained to lie within some particular subset of the plane—for example, a disk, a closed triangular region, or along a curve. We saw an instance of this situation in Example 6 of the previous section. Here we explore a powerful method for finding extreme values of constrained functions: the method of Lagrange multipliers."},{"x":0.0992,"y":0.55333,"w":0.1615,"h":0.01207,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Historical Biography"},{"x":0.0992,"y":0.56897,"w":0.13899,"h":0.02551,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Joseph Louis Lagrange (1736–1813)"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.63057,"w":0.25254,"h":0.01658,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Constrained Maxima and Minima"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.65553,"w":0.59294,"h":0.02962,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"To gain some insight, we first consider a problem where a constrained minimum can be found by eliminating a variable."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.71475,"w":0.58892,"h":0.03179,"fs":0.01407,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Example 1 Find the point p(x, y, z) on the plane 2x + y - z - 5 = 0 that is clos- est to the origin."},{"x":0.51087,"y":0.73865,"w":0.29483,"h":0.10245,"fs":0.01353,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"0 r OP 0 = 2(x - 0)2 + ( y - 0)2 + (z - 0)2"},{"x":0.55399,"y":0.76167,"w":0.12123,"h":0.08776,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= 2x2 + y2 + z2"},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.76451,"w":0.48866,"h":0.01542,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Solution The problem asks us to find the minimum value of the function"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.84993,"w":0.18448,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"subject to the constraint that"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.86351,"w":0.36707,"h":0.0776,"fs":0.01353,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Since 0 r OP 0 has a minimum value wherever the function"},{"x":0.58363,"y":0.87232,"w":0.14686,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"2x + y - z - 5 = 0."},{"x":0.57321,"y":0.91389,"w":0.16769,"h":0.0217,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"ƒ(x, y, z) = x2 + y2 + z2"}]}